==Icelandic==

===Etymology===
From {{m|is|ég||I, the personal pronoun}} and {{m|is|heiti||I'm called}}, first person form of {{m|is|heita||to be called, to be named}}. Literally meaning "I am called" or "I am named".

===Phrase===
{{head|is|phrase|head=[[ég#Icelandic|ég]] [[heita#Icelandic|heiti]]}}

# [[I]] [[am]]; [[my name is]]
#: {{ux|is|'''Ég heiti''' Ríkharður.|'''My name is''' Richard.}}
#: {{ux|is|'''Ég heiti''' Braga, [[hvað heitir þú]]?|'''My name is''' Braga, [[what's your name]]?}}

